#英文摘要(关键词: ("SpringBoot", "University Course Scheduling", "Intelligent System; Genetic Algorithm", "Frontend and Backend Separation"))[
  University timetabling requires the coordination of courses, instructors, classrooms, and student groups under constraints on time conflicts and resource capacity. This thesis presents the design of an intelligent university timetabling system based on Spring Boot. The system uses a separate frontend and backend and includes modules for data management, scheduling configuration, conflict detection, timetable queries, and manual adjustments. 
  
  System requirements, technology choices, data structures, and the scheduling workflow are described to support implementation and testing. This abstract is sample text for the template; the final thesis should report the methods, test conditions, and results of the actual study.

  
